// @run
// @log 2
// @log 3
// @hint Intentionally-unused variable `_p`
// @hint Intentionally-unused variable `_r`
// The generic-application NOMINAL sidecar (typed-IR P1), on the two shapes its reverse map
// has to render that the sibling `…-inline-frontier.vl` does not: a TWO-ARGUMENT head
// (`Pair<i32,string>` — exercising the argument JOIN, which must be `,` with no space, the
// spelling `gaeArgsTextOf` cuts on and `canonEmitName` keeps, so an agreeing render is
// byte-equal rather than merely equivalent) and a NON-i32 argument (`Box<string>`).
//
// Both cells REJECTED at emit before the sidecar ("ref valtype with no interned shape"),
// for the reason recorded on the frontier fixture: the shape-registration walk is
// arena-driven and registered the EXPANDED key while every classifier looked the shape up
// under the application name canon had left on the inline member.
//
// A THIRD shape is deliberately absent. `const q: Box<i32>[] = [{v: 5}]` alongside a
// `Box<string> | Tag` binding writes INVALID WASM ("type mismatch: expected i32, found
// (ref $type)") — and it does so on MASTER too, with no generic application interned at
// all, so it is a pre-existing ref-list/union-arm defect and not this sidecar's to carry.
// `Box<i32>[]` on its own builds and runs identically on both sides.
type Box<T> = { v: T }
type Pair<A, B> = { a: A, b: B }
type Tag = { t: i32 }

const _p: Pair<i32, string> | Tag = { a: 7, b: "x" }
print(2)

const _r: Box<string> | Tag = { v: "hi" }
print(3)
